-- Task draw-tuple-destructuring-evaluates-rhs-twice: the ticket's own repro.
-- `a` and `b` come from one draw of a perfectly correlated pair, so they always
-- agree. When the tuple pattern evaluated the definition once per component,
-- this was 0.5. The `if` wrapper is a no-op; the bare `a == b` spelling is
-- refused for a reason unrelated to destructuring (`draw c = ... in c == c` is
-- refused the same way).
main = draw (a, b) = (if Uniform < 0.5 then (True, True) else (False, False)) in if a == b then True else False
